To demonstrate compliance with COBS Rule 14.2.12(a) for weekly reconciliations of Client Money, the following records must be maintained:  
- Weekly reconciliation reports showing the reconciliation of Client Money in Client Accounts;  
- Records of Client Accounts (as required by COBS Rule 14.6.2 and 15.4.3);  
- Records of the most recent reconciliations of Client Money (as required by COBS Rule 14.11.1 and 15.9.1);  
- Documentation of procedures and controls in place to ensure the accuracy and integrity of the reconciliation process;  
- Records of any discrepancies identified during reconciliations and how they were resolved;  
- Records related to the Auditor's Report (COBS Rule 7.6.6(1)(g)) regarding material discrepancies in reconciliations;  
- Records of Client classification and agreements (COBS Rule 2.7.1 and 3.7.1(d)).
